{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791563145,"nonce":"gb74gMGeH5PLyGIXCnWKxLVNhZ0=","title":"Shared CSS engine: parsing, selectors, cascade and a compiled sheet format","message":"One CSS engine for every SDK, in blinc_abi, built on Blinc's blinc_css: ashui (Haxe) and blinc_ts (TypeScript) parse, match and cascade with the same code, so a stylesheet behaves the same whichever SDK runs it, and the cost of matching and cascading is native.\n\n**Scope**\n- Parsing: the CSS ashui supports today (ashui haxe/ashui/css: CssParser, Selector, Stylesheet, Media, Animations, PointerQueries, UserAgent; about 6,400 lines of Haxe to match), with diagnostics carrying file, line and column, errors and warnings apart. @import, custom properties, @media, @keyframes, transitions, the shape properties (corner smoothing and exponent).\n- Selectors: type, class, id, attribute, compound and combinators, the state pseudo-classes (:hover, :active, :focus, :focus-visible, :checked, :disabled, form states), structural ones (:first-child, :nth-child, :empty, :has), :not, :is, :where.\n- Cascade: origins (user-agent, library, page), specificity and order, inheritance, var() with fallbacks, applied to a LayoutContext's nodes through the property router, so the result lands where layout and paint read it. Restyle is incremental: a class, attribute, state or custom-property change restyles the nodes it can affect, not the tree.\n- A compiled sheet format: the parsed sheet as a versioned, compact binary that loads without parsing. It is what compile-time CSS produces in every SDK.\n\n**Compile-time CSS in each SDK, with the same compiler**\n- A small command-line compiler from this crate (for example `blinc-css compile in.css`) prints diagnostics with positions and writes the compiled sheet.\n- ashui: the CompiledCss macro runs it through sys.io.Process, reports its diagnostics as compile errors and warnings at their line in the .css file (as today), and embeds the compiled sheet with Context.addResource. At run time the bytes go to native. Haxe macros cannot load a native library, so the tool is a separate binary, shipped prebuilt with the haxelib.\n- blinc_ts: the Vite plugin calls the same compiler through the addon at build time and emits the compiled sheet as a module; it can also emit types for the class names a sheet defines.\n\n**Order**\n1. Parser and compiled format, with the CLI, checked against ashui's CSS tests.\n2. Selector matching and cascade on LayoutContext, with incremental restyle.\n3. N-API bindings (blinc_ts 6e33649) and the HashLink exports.\n4. ashui moves its cascade onto it (a follow-up there; ashui keeps its own until then).","files":null}]}